# GemGrade Development Workflow

Maintain production-quality software. Every completed task follows this workflow.

## Quality check (before done)

- Application builds successfully
- No new linting errors
- No obvious runtime errors
- Mobile and desktop layouts verified
- Modified files reviewed; no unrelated files changed
- UI stays consistent with GemGrade design language
- Clear, low-risk improvements: implement them

## Git workflow (after work)

1. Review all changed files
2. Create a descriptive git commit
3. Push to the current development branch
4. Summarize: what changed, files modified, commit hash, recommendations

Commit messages must be descriptive (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `style:`). Never: `update`, `fix`, `changes`, `misc`.

This workflow authorizes commit + push after each completed task. Follow commit safety (no force push, no secrets, no config tampering).

## Production safety

- Never merge into the production branch
- Never deploy to production
- Never overwrite production configuration
- Never remove existing functionality unless explicitly instructed
- Production deployments require explicit approval from the project owner

## Engineering mindset

Before every commit: *Would I be proud if this shipped to thousands of collectors?* If no, keep improving. Leave the project better than you found it. Build software collectors will trust.
